{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For nothing is reduced, etc.</b> The reason it says ״כִּי אֵין״ etc. and does not say ״וְאֵין נִגְרָע״ — its meaning is thus: Thus said Pharaoh, etc., <b>you go</b> etc. — and these words contain no evil tidings; on the contrary, they would desire the matter, to lighten from them the labor of building and to do this work of gathering stubble for straw. Therefore he stated the reason for the decree, which is <b>for nothing is reduced</b> — and this is nothing but reducing the time for this matter, so that you will do your labor in a short time."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:49.253321565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}